# Line endings. LF, everywhere, on every platform.
#
# This file is the guard CodeBrix.LilyScheme already carries and this repository was
# missing. Without it, a Windows clone under `core.autocrlf=true` expands 4,545 of the
# 5,328 tracked files to CRLF on the way out, and the port does not work at all:
#
#   Scheme error: read-error
#     (#f "lily/lily.scm:430:1: invalid character in escape sequence: ~S" (#\return) #f)
#
# scm/lily.scm:430 ends a string with a backslash line continuation, the CR lands where
# an escape character is expected, and lily.scm dies on its first form. The 55-file
# startup layer never loads, so `markup?', `ly:load' and `lyric-event' are unbound and
# 312 of the 2,608 tests fail. Measured 2026-08-31: a CRLF checkout fails 314, an LF
# checkout of the same commit on the same machine fails 2.
#
# It is not only a local inconvenience. Everything under Scheme/ and the parser mirror
# is an <EmbeddedResource>, so whatever bytes are on disk at build time are baked into
# the assembly and shipped in the NuGet package -- packing on a CRLF checkout produces
# a .nupkg that is broken for every consumer, on every platform.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF. These rules only stop a checkout from expanding
# them, which also keeps the vendored and mirrored files byte-identical to their
# upstream originals so a re-sync stays a straight copy plus cmp.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Baked into the assembly: src/CodeBrix.LilyPort.Engine/Scheme/** is embedded
# wholesale, and CRLF here is a broken shipped artifact rather than a test failure.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.scm   text eol=lf
*.ly    text eol=lf
*.ily   text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf

# The SVG music fonts are embedded too, and SvgFontOutlines parses their glyph paths.
*.svg   text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The mirrors, kept byte-identical to the pinned LilyPond 2.27.2 sources.
# parser.yy and lexer.ll are embedded AND pinned by SHA-256: GrammarShapeTests
# hashes them, and the recorded digests are over LF bytes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.yy    text eol=lf
*.ll    text eol=lf
*.mf    text eol=lf
*.mp    text eol=lf

# Documentation/MANIFEST.sha256 records a digest for each of 690 mirrored files, and
# Lily.Docs' CorpusMirrorTests checks every one of them.
*.itely text eol=lf
*.itexi text eol=lf
*.tely  text eol=lf
*.texi  text eol=lf
*.bib   text eol=lf
*.bst   text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
Documentation/**/README text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test fixtures. The parity suites replay recorded inputs and compare the output
# character for character, so a stray CR is a diff.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.json  text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.abc   text eol=lf
*.eps   text eol=lf
*.snippet-list text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sources and scripts. Not load-bearing for the suites, but a repository with one
# convention has no second convention to get wrong.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.cs      text eol=lf
*.csproj  text eol=lf
*.slnx    text eol=lf
*.shproj  text eol=lf
*.projitems text eol=lf
*.xaml    text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.pl      text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
*.conf    text eol=lf
*.in      text eol=lf
*.mdc     text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.clinerules    text eol=lf
.cursorrules   text eol=lf
.windsurfrules text eol=lf
LICENSE        text eol=lf
LICENSE.OFL    text eol=lf
COPYING.FDL    text eol=lf
*.LICENSE      text eol=lf
*.COPYING      text eol=lf
tools/parser-baseline/parser.output text eol=lf
mf/GNUmakefile text eol=lf
tools/Lily.Docs/assets/staged/ROADMAP text eol=lf
tests/CodeBrix.LilyPort.Tests/fixtures/musicxml/inputs/LICENSE text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never touched. Declared rather than left to git's heuristic, because a font or a
# MIDI file that gets newline translation applied to it is silently corrupt.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.otf   binary
*.png   binary
*.PNG   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.midi  binary
*.mxl   binary
